#N canvas 20 20 2100 1350 12;
#X text 20 20 c_kit -- the drums \, played in Pd: sixteen c_voice \, one a pad \, each with its distortion inside it and an e_delay beside it \, and one e_verb they all send to \, summed into its outlet~. It takes the pad messages c_steps sends \, so the sequencer and the drum page play it as they played the SP-404. ref/module/sequencer.md, f 70;
#X text 20 130 creation args: none. inlet: pad <1..16> <velocity> \, a pad past 16 ignored \, and from c_steps a track's vol <pad> <dB> and pitch <pad> <semitones> and its effects: drive \, tone and dist (the distortion's mix) <pad> <0-100> and char <pad> <1-4> \, its character \, to its voice \, delay-time <pad> <steps> and feedback <pad> <0-100> to its e_delay \, delay (the level) and send <pad> <0-100> to both \, send to e_verb too \, and size and damping <0-100> and verb-type <0-2>: plate \, gigaverb or freeverb \, as e_verb's type \, to e_verb \, and a held repeat's tape <span> <units> and tape-off to e_tape. outlet~: the voices \, the delays and the reverb or its loop \, summed \, mono -- u_root adds them to the left output \, where the OLED's meter reads them with the mic (ref/module/audio.md). At load it reports on err how many of the sixteen samples it found (C-12)., f 70;
