#X text 1300 1040 The tempo bus's BPM \, clamped as u_tempo clamps it \, as a step's length in ms \, a sixteenth: each e_delay's time follows it., f 50;
#X text 1100 560 The effects (Brendan \, 2026-11-05): a distortion in each voice \, a delay beside each \, and one reverb for all sixteen \, since sixteen are more than the Organelle can afford. Each has a switch~ that keeps it off while its mix \, level or every send is 0 \, once a delay's or the reverb's tail has died \, so an effect unused costs nothing. They reach each other by throw~ and catch~ \, not cords: a switched-off abstraction with a signal inlet or outlet still costs a copy every block \, and sixteen e_delays and their cords cost 2% of the Organelle's core at rest (ref/module/sequencer.md). The voices' dry sound stays on its cords \, as it was. The sixteen e_delays sit in one e_delays \, whose own switch~ is off while all of them are \, so at rest they are skipped once a block \, not sixteen times., f 60;
#X text 20 1060 DSP order: these boxes come after the voices in the file \, so they run before them \, the delays first \, then the reverb \, then the catch~ (ref/module/sequencer.md \, The effects)., f 60;
